{"url": "https://www.vsmath.at/", "final_url": "https://www.vsmath.at/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-31", "text": "VSM\nSkip to content\nHome\nAbout VSM\nMission\nOrganization\nStudying in the VSM\nCalls & Positions\nMedia presence\nPeople\nExecutive Board\nUNIVIE Steering Committee\nStudent Board\nStudents\nAlumni\nActivities & Benefits\nMini Courses\nSummer/Winter Schools\nStudent Retreats\nPhD Colloquia\nWorkshops & Other Events\nMental Health\nMentoring program\nFinancial support\nRegular course program\nCurrent Call\nContact\nProject Coordinators\nTeam\nSearch this website\nMen\u00fc\nSchlie\u00dfen\nHome\nAbout VSM\nMission\nOrganization\nStudying in the VSM\nCalls & Positions\nMedia presence\nPeople\nExecutive Board\nUNIVIE Steering Committee\nStudent Board\nStudents\nAlumni\nActivities & Benefits\nMini Courses\nSummer/Winter Schools\nStudent Retreats\nPhD Colloquia\nWorkshops & Other Events\nMental Health\nMentoring program\nFinancial support\nRegular course program\nCurrent Call\nContact\nProject Coordinators\nTeam\nUniversity of Vienna\nThe Vienna School of Mathematics\nis a joint doctoral school of the University of Vienna and TU Wien.\nOur mission is to provide a top-level scientific training of doctoral students in all fields of mathematics and to foster a vibrant and supportive community for all these students. We are committed to offering clear structures and quality criteria and to ensure that our doctoral candidates receive the support they need to thrive.\nThe VSM is also intended to serve as a hub to attract outstanding mathematics students from across Europe and around the world to Vienna, guiding them towards research at the forefront of modern mathematics. By creating an exciting and dynamic scientific environment, we aim to inspire groundbreaking research and shape the next\ngeneration of mathematical researchers.\nTU Wien\nImprint\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy policy\n\u00a9 Vienna School of Mathematics", "links": [["Skip to c